1
00:00:49,115 --> 00:00:50,673
Raaargh!

2
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:17,467
Seize their hand bags.

3
00:01:17,544 --> 00:01:21,981
Oi! A little of what you have
could be a lot for the poor of Nottingham.

4
00:01:22,048 --> 00:01:25,484
- We are the poor.
- Let them take what they need.

5
00:01:27,854 --> 00:01:29,549
Dad?

6
00:01:29,622 --> 00:01:32,591
Dad! It's me!

7
00:01:40,233 --> 00:01:41,894
Will, you know these people?

8
00:01:42,001 --> 00:01:44,799
Meet my father, Dan Scarlett.

9
00:01:44,871 --> 00:01:47,101
And my little brother, Lukey.

10
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:50,699
- I'm not little.
- My big little brother, Lukey.

11
00:02:33,686 --> 00:02:35,813
So what brings you back to Nottingham?

12
00:02:35,889 --> 00:02:38,449
We're going to take Will
back to Scarborough.

13
00:02:38,558 --> 00:02:40,822
- What?
- Hey.

14
00:02:40,894 --> 00:02:43,590
What about asking me if I want to come?

15
00:02:43,663 --> 00:02:47,531
- We're your family.
- I've got a family here, too, Dad.

16
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:50,569
We were sure you'd come and find us.
Didn't you miss us?

17
00:02:50,637 --> 00:02:53,231
Yeah, but...

18
00:02:53,306 --> 00:02:55,240
I'm with Robin now.

19
00:02:56,442 --> 00:02:58,672
"I'm with Robin now"?

20
00:02:58,778 --> 00:03:02,339
Son, you've got
your whole life ahead of you.

21
00:03:15,728 --> 00:03:18,891
- What's that?
- It's a letter.

22
00:03:18,998 --> 00:03:21,193
Yeah, but to who?

23
00:03:21,267 --> 00:03:23,201
It's to the King.

24
00:03:23,269 --> 00:03:26,170
- What about?
- The Sheriff and the Black Knights.

25
00:03:26,239 --> 00:03:30,107
- Who's delivering it?
- An old friend.

26
00:03:30,210 --> 00:03:32,804
- Roger of Stoke.
- Roger.

27
00:03:35,615 --> 00:03:38,846
- Where are you meeting him?
- How many questions have you got?!

28
00:03:38,918 --> 00:03:40,579
I'm just curious.

29
00:03:40,653 --> 00:03:43,645
I'm meeting him in Nottingham,
after the money drop.

30
00:03:46,392 --> 00:03:48,417
This craftsmanship is good.

31
00:03:48,494 --> 00:03:51,224
See - I've got a life here.

32
00:03:51,297 --> 00:03:55,097
All that says to me is you could earn
a decent living in Scarborough.

33
00:03:55,201 --> 00:03:56,600
Dad, I'm an outlaw.

34
00:03:56,669 --> 00:03:59,570
- I stand up for what I believe in.
- What, and I don't?

35
00:03:59,639 --> 00:04:02,403
- It doesn't matter.
- Yes, it does. Tell me.

36
00:04:02,475 --> 00:04:06,206
- You let the Sheriff cut off your hand.
- That was to save me and you.

37
00:04:06,279 --> 00:04:08,941
- I know, I didn't mean that.
- Yes, you did.

38
00:04:12,185 --> 00:04:15,552
Robin, tell me father I'm a grown man.
I make my own decisions.

39
00:04:15,622 --> 00:04:18,182
A real man listens to advice, Will.

40
00:04:20,159 --> 00:04:23,128
- Thanks, Robin.
- But Will does have a life here.

41
00:04:23,196 --> 00:04:26,563
And you should see it
before you take him away from it.

42
00:04:26,633 --> 00:04:29,397
Come to Nottingham tomorrow,
let us show you what we do.

43
00:04:35,508 --> 00:04:39,035
Look, it's him.
Jess, it is the Nightwatchman.

44
00:04:51,691 --> 00:04:54,956
Let's see. What did he bring?

45
00:04:55,028 --> 00:04:57,121
God bless you, Nightwatchman.

46
00:05:03,836 --> 00:05:08,068
"And that night... the Angel of the Lord
went back and forth. "

47
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:12,869
Mmm.

48
00:05:17,884 --> 00:05:20,580
Ah! The Nightwatchman.

49
00:05:21,621 --> 00:05:25,489
So... how was your evening's generosity?

50
00:05:25,591 --> 00:05:28,560
Very satisfying. They all took the bait.

51
00:05:28,628 --> 00:05:30,186
Like rats.

52
00:05:30,263 --> 00:05:31,628
Good.

53
00:05:33,199 --> 00:05:38,535
Shouldn't you be, um, measuring
or whatever it is you do?

54
00:05:38,604 --> 00:05:41,038
- Scientific analysis.
- Quite, hmm.

55
00:05:41,107 --> 00:05:43,541
I'm waiting to be caught in the quarantine.

56
00:05:43,609 --> 00:05:46,635
Ah! Yes.

57
00:05:48,181 --> 00:05:51,673
The er... pestilent poor of Pitt Street.

58
00:05:52,618 --> 00:05:54,882
Off you go.

59
00:06:03,796 --> 00:06:06,560
Please! Please, jailer,
let me see my father.

60
00:06:06,632 --> 00:06:10,534
- Can't be done. I've told you.
- Marian, I am well.

61
00:06:11,604 --> 00:06:14,004
- I will speak to the Sheriff.
- Do not worry.

62
00:06:14,073 --> 00:06:17,008
- Speak away, my dear.
- Sheriff!

63
00:06:18,478 --> 00:06:21,276
This punishment hurts my father, not me.

64
00:06:21,381 --> 00:06:24,145
Ooh, I don't know, I think it hurts you both.

65
00:06:24,217 --> 00:06:25,878
It is efficient.

66
00:06:25,985 --> 00:06:29,284
Make you think
before you undermine my authority again,

67
00:06:29,389 --> 00:06:33,120
which, trust me, is in your best interests.

68
00:06:34,660 --> 00:06:36,958
Please! Please, Sheriff.

69
00:06:37,029 --> 00:06:39,759
There must be something I can do. Guy?

70
00:06:39,832 --> 00:06:44,428
It's no good making those big eyes at him.
He doesn't want you any more.

71
00:06:46,105 --> 00:06:49,165
Tell you what. You read this
announcement for me

72
00:06:49,242 --> 00:06:52,837
and we'll see if we can
get Daddy some dinner.

73
00:06:52,912 --> 00:06:55,073
You mean, you haven't fed him?

74
00:06:58,251 --> 00:06:59,513
Sheriff!

75
00:07:00,953 --> 00:07:03,421
Right. Time to spread a bit of...

76
00:07:03,489 --> 00:07:05,889
- Happiness.
... happiness. That's right.

77
00:07:05,958 --> 00:07:08,586
Time to spread a bit of happiness.

78
00:07:15,034 --> 00:07:16,626
Bless you.

79
00:07:16,702 --> 00:07:20,570
- You see, these people need us.
- We need you, too, your family.

80
00:07:22,108 --> 00:07:24,668
Help me!
Somebody, please, help me.

81
00:07:24,777 --> 00:07:27,769
Robin, Robin, help.

82
00:07:27,847 --> 00:07:31,578
It's Jess - she's got something.
I think it's the pestilence.

83
00:07:31,651 --> 00:07:33,812
Will, get Djaq.

84
00:07:36,456 --> 00:07:39,084
No swellings.
How long has she been like this?

85
00:07:39,192 --> 00:07:40,887
Since this morning.

86
00:07:40,993 --> 00:07:42,585
Toot-ti-toot.

87
00:07:51,504 --> 00:07:54,371
- People of Nottingham...
- Louder.

88
00:07:55,908 --> 00:07:58,809
- People of Nottingham!
- Good.

89
00:07:58,878 --> 00:08:02,871
On behalf of the Sheriff,
I make the following announcement.

90
00:08:02,982 --> 00:08:05,041
The pestilence has come to Nottingham.

91
00:08:06,719 --> 00:08:09,210
- My God, that's what it is.
- No, it's not.

92
00:08:09,288 --> 00:08:14,021
Do not be afraid. It is confined
to the houses in Pitt Street.

93
00:08:14,093 --> 00:08:16,561
There will be a quarantine in place.

94
00:08:16,629 --> 00:08:19,462
No one is to pass through
without permission.

95
00:08:19,532 --> 00:08:22,592
No one is to pass food or medicine...

96
00:08:22,668 --> 00:08:24,829
What? There's young ones suffering.

97
00:08:24,904 --> 00:08:27,498
They can't be cut off with nothing!

98
00:08:27,573 --> 00:08:31,976
To do so risks spreading the infection

99
00:08:32,044 --> 00:08:34,205
and will be punished by death.

100
00:08:39,118 --> 00:08:42,815
- She's gonna die!
- No, she isn't. That's not what she's got.

101
00:08:42,889 --> 00:08:44,823
Sarah, take Jess home.

102
00:08:44,891 --> 00:08:46,825
Djaq and I will come soon.

103
00:08:46,893 --> 00:08:51,353
- Be careful.
- We will not be cowed by this infection.

104
00:08:51,430 --> 00:08:53,364
Business will continue as normal.

105
00:08:53,432 --> 00:08:56,526
- All workers are to report...
- What's Marian's game?

106
00:08:56,602 --> 00:09:00,333
- She's just doing what she's told.
... at their usual hour.

107
00:09:00,406 --> 00:09:06,174
Now... you may hear cries for help,
pleas for mercy, medicine -

108
00:09:06,245 --> 00:09:08,839
"Help me! Help me, help me!"

109
00:09:08,915 --> 00:09:10,439
Word of advice.

110
00:09:16,188 --> 00:09:17,849
Go forth in peace.

111
00:09:17,924 --> 00:09:21,587
Robin, he's condemning
the whole street to death.

112
00:09:21,661 --> 00:09:23,458
Love, serve... your Sheriff.

113
00:09:25,464 --> 00:09:27,455
Sheriff, this is not right!

114
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:29,933
Dan! Dan!

115
00:09:31,170 --> 00:09:33,934
- What?
- I've just looked at a young lass.

116
00:09:34,006 --> 00:09:36,998
- It's not a pestilence.
- Shut him up.

117
00:09:37,076 --> 00:09:40,136
I've seen a pestilence before
in Scarborough.

118
00:09:40,212 --> 00:09:43,147
These people must have food and water.

119
00:09:43,215 --> 00:09:44,944
And medicines.

120
00:09:45,017 --> 00:09:50,250
- I said shut up.
- I've shut up for you once before.

121
00:09:50,323 --> 00:09:53,588
It cost me my wife, my hand
and the respect of my son,

122
00:09:53,659 --> 00:09:55,388
so I'm not shutting up any more.

123
00:09:55,461 --> 00:09:57,622
Why are you saying this is a pestilence?

124
00:09:58,798 --> 00:10:00,425
Dad!

125
00:10:13,412 --> 00:10:15,812
Well done.

126
00:10:15,881 --> 00:10:18,179
Hysteria! Panic!

127
00:10:19,652 --> 00:10:22,382
In times of crisis, not very helpful.

128
00:10:22,455 --> 00:10:24,355
It will not be tolerated.

129
00:10:28,661 --> 00:10:31,630
- Will, you can't go up there.
- I'll kill him now.

130
00:10:31,697 --> 00:10:33,824
You heard the Sheriff.

131
00:10:33,899 --> 00:10:36,026
Set up those barricades.

132
00:10:36,135 --> 00:10:39,161
- There's too many of them, Will.
- I don't care!

133
00:10:39,238 --> 00:10:41,229
Will!

134
00:10:44,076 --> 00:10:46,772
Come on, move yourselves!

135
00:10:52,918 --> 00:10:56,285
- We need to go to Pitt Street.
- Pitt Street? What?

136
00:10:56,389 --> 00:10:59,051
There are people there, our people,

137
00:10:59,125 --> 00:11:01,685
and they need us.

138
00:11:01,794 --> 00:11:03,659
- Djaq.
- Of course.

139
00:11:03,729 --> 00:11:07,631
- Robin... The pestilence!
- I'm not sure, either, to be honest.

140
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:10,794
I think Dan was right -
there is no pestilence.

141
00:11:10,870 --> 00:11:14,169
- That's why the Sheriff killed him.
- "You think"?

142
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:15,969
No! Help!

143
00:11:16,042 --> 00:11:19,739
We haven't got time.
They're setting the barricades up right now.

144
00:11:19,812 --> 00:11:21,245
Help! Please help us.

145
00:11:21,313 --> 00:11:24,282
- Come on.
- I'll do the letter for whatshisname.

146
00:11:24,383 --> 00:11:26,783
- Roger of Stoke.
- Good thinking.

147
00:11:26,852 --> 00:11:29,446
Here - go.

148
00:11:29,522 --> 00:11:32,753
The rest of you, I can't ask you
to risk your lives

149
00:11:32,825 --> 00:11:35,658
but if you do come with
me, then do it for Dan.

150
00:11:35,728 --> 00:11:37,662
Now, come on.

151
00:11:41,434 --> 00:11:44,426
Will, Pitt Street by the back way, now.

152
00:11:50,876 --> 00:11:53,140
Go on! Move it!

153
00:11:56,982 --> 00:11:59,780
Put your backs into it.

154
00:12:09,195 --> 00:12:12,790
Let me through. I don't live here.
I was just walking this way.

155
00:12:12,865 --> 00:12:16,266
- I'm from Leicester.
- Sheriff's orders!

156
00:12:16,368 --> 00:12:18,802
This has got nothing to do with me.

157
00:12:18,871 --> 00:12:22,034
Don't do this! Don't do this!
My Jess needs help.

158
00:12:22,141 --> 00:12:23,699
Sarah!

159
00:12:23,776 --> 00:12:24,936
Robin!

160
00:12:25,010 --> 00:12:27,706
No, no, you can't be here,
you'll never get out.

161
00:12:27,780 --> 00:12:30,943
- I said I'd come and find you.
- Take us to your daughter.

162
00:12:31,016 --> 00:12:33,610
Let's see what we can do, come on.

163
00:12:45,598 --> 00:12:47,657
She needs water, lots of water.

164
00:12:47,733 --> 00:12:50,827
Are there any other people affected?

165
00:12:50,903 --> 00:12:53,167
Half the houses in the street.

166
00:12:57,243 --> 00:13:00,974
Right, I want beds and clean linens...

167
00:13:01,380 --> 00:13:03,439
all in one place. Go.

168
00:13:04,316 --> 00:13:08,252
And all the herbs and medicines from
every house brought here to Djaq.

169
00:13:09,221 --> 00:13:11,382
Hey, hey, hey.

170
00:13:11,457 --> 00:13:14,358
Luke... Luke, your dad wouldn't want this.

171
00:13:14,426 --> 00:13:16,223
How do you know what he'd want?

172
00:13:16,295 --> 00:13:20,459
- I should've killed the Sheriff.
- You can't just kill the Sheriff.

173
00:13:20,533 --> 00:13:24,663
Prince John would send an army
to destroy Nottingham. It would create hell.

174
00:13:24,737 --> 00:13:30,232
Robin, I'm gonna take him home,
back to Scarborough.

175
00:13:30,309 --> 00:13:32,243
I don't want him to get even.

176
00:13:32,311 --> 00:13:34,677
- If you need us here...
- No, no.

177
00:13:36,849 --> 00:13:40,785
No, take him. When you return,
we'll honor your father.

178
00:13:40,853 --> 00:13:41,877
Thank you.

179
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:57,428
- Where's Sarah?
- Don't you know? She lives in Pitt Street.

180
00:13:57,503 --> 00:13:59,801
- Is she affected?
- Little Jess.

181
00:14:02,541 --> 00:14:05,999
Right. We must get them medicine.

182
00:14:06,078 --> 00:14:08,205
And I need your clothes.

183
00:14:13,185 --> 00:14:15,847
- I'm sorry, Will.
- Me too, Robin.

184
00:14:18,424 --> 00:14:20,619
Really sorry.

185
00:15:14,380 --> 00:15:18,407
- We'll need to take food, as well.
- No need, miss. They're all fed.

186
00:15:18,484 --> 00:15:22,420
The Nightwatchman visited last night -
Pitt Street.

187
00:15:27,426 --> 00:15:29,951
- Don't come in.
- Marian?

188
00:15:30,029 --> 00:15:33,521
You can't come in.

189
00:15:35,701 --> 00:15:40,604
- I cannot talk to you through the door.
- Then you cannot talk to me at all.

190
00:15:40,673 --> 00:15:45,610
I wanted to apologize for what happened
today, the way you were treated.

191
00:15:45,678 --> 00:15:49,512
Am I to perform like a monkey
whilst my father starves in the dungeon?

192
00:15:49,581 --> 00:15:54,143
- No. I will see that your father is fed.
- Really?

193
00:15:54,219 --> 00:15:58,155
- And what do you want in return?
- Nothing.

194
00:15:59,525 --> 00:16:03,393
- You have my word.
- Then thank you.

195
00:16:03,462 --> 00:16:06,625
Marian... please...

196
00:16:06,699 --> 00:16:08,599
let me in.

197
00:16:18,610 --> 00:16:22,171
- The Nightwatchman went to Pitt Street?
- Yes.

198
00:16:24,249 --> 00:16:28,015
Hello? It's Robin Hood.
Do you have any medicines or herbs?

199
00:16:29,688 --> 00:16:33,624
Robin, please, go away. We have
the pestilence here. Save yourself.

200
00:16:39,932 --> 00:16:42,958
- What are you doing?
- I'm helping the sick.

201
00:16:43,035 --> 00:16:44,969
Leave them alone.

202
00:16:45,037 --> 00:16:48,097
I mean... you could die.

203
00:16:49,475 --> 00:16:52,501
That's a risk I take every day.

204
00:16:53,746 --> 00:16:56,078
You know what? You're right. Forgive me.

205
00:16:56,181 --> 00:16:58,240
Look, let me help.

206
00:16:59,551 --> 00:17:03,351
- What's your name?
- Joseph. I'm here by mistake.

207
00:17:03,422 --> 00:17:05,515
You're from Leicester - I heard.

208
00:17:05,591 --> 00:17:08,253
Did you see how
those men treated me? Godless.

209
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:11,727
Well, welcome to Nottingham.

210
00:17:11,797 --> 00:17:14,391
Er, Robin.

211
00:17:14,466 --> 00:17:17,435
These men are with me.
Can you help them?

212
00:17:23,242 --> 00:17:24,937
These people are burning up.

213
00:17:25,010 --> 00:17:28,377
Perhaps it would be a kindness
just not to interfere,

214
00:17:28,447 --> 00:17:30,813
not prolong the pain.

215
00:17:31,216 --> 00:17:34,583
This is a medicine chest.
Every medicine known to man

216
00:17:34,653 --> 00:17:36,518
and some unknown.

217
00:17:38,257 --> 00:17:40,589
- Oh, don't do that.
- Why not?

218
00:17:40,659 --> 00:17:44,060
I'm a man, you're a woman.
I fall in love very easily.

219
00:17:44,163 --> 00:17:46,063
Don't worry. I don't.

220
00:17:55,607 --> 00:17:59,566
I'll make sure it's safe.
I know what to look for better than you.

221
00:17:59,645 --> 00:18:02,671
Why do you always treat me
like I'm a baby?

222
00:18:16,495 --> 00:18:18,827
I love you, Luke.

223
00:18:18,897 --> 00:18:20,888
See? Your turn.

224
00:18:25,537 --> 00:18:29,166
- Will?
- Run away. Run back to Scarborough.

225
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:34,170
This place is about to turn into hell.

226
00:18:34,246 --> 00:18:36,043
Will! Will!

227
00:18:36,115 --> 00:18:37,639
Will!

228
00:18:44,156 --> 00:18:47,455
- She'll not die, will she?
- Not if I can help it.

229
00:18:47,559 --> 00:18:49,993
You're from the fourth house
on the street?

230
00:18:50,062 --> 00:18:52,826
And he ate a pie last night
and nothing since?

231
00:18:52,898 --> 00:18:54,559
That's right.

232
00:18:56,235 --> 00:18:58,135
- Good.
- Good?

233
00:19:03,041 --> 00:19:05,407
She's hotter - look at the cheeks and lips.

234
00:19:05,477 --> 00:19:08,344
- Are you trained in medicine?
- Me? No.

235
00:19:08,413 --> 00:19:12,076
I'm just... I'm just hoping
this poor child recovers.

236
00:19:15,954 --> 00:19:17,717
Dougal!

237
00:19:42,114 --> 00:19:45,208
Stand or you're dead.

238
00:20:09,508 --> 00:20:11,976
Phew!

239
00:20:13,445 --> 00:20:15,845
- A shame.
- A shame?

240
00:20:18,417 --> 00:20:21,284
It's an outrage. That's another life wasted.

241
00:20:21,386 --> 00:20:25,948
- Do you suspect foul play?
- Joseph! Joseph, this is Nottingham.

242
00:20:26,024 --> 00:20:28,549
There is no other kind of play.

243
00:20:36,468 --> 00:20:38,663
Will! You scared me.

244
00:20:38,770 --> 00:20:41,762
Why are you here?
Do you have a message from Robin?

245
00:20:42,841 --> 00:20:44,365
Will?

246
00:20:45,010 --> 00:20:46,170
Will!

247
00:20:51,984 --> 00:20:53,781
So...

248
00:20:53,852 --> 00:20:57,811
you're all from different families
and you haven't eaten together.

249
00:20:57,889 --> 00:21:01,017
We've all eaten the pies, though.
Our Jess ate ours.

250
00:21:01,093 --> 00:21:04,256
- How much did she have?
- What pies?

251
00:21:04,363 --> 00:21:06,388
The Nightwatchman's.

252
00:21:07,399 --> 00:21:11,768
- He brought them last night, every house.
- Soup - I'll make everybody soup.

253
00:21:14,473 --> 00:21:16,839
They're dropping like flies, my lord.

254
00:21:18,010 --> 00:21:21,377
The poison's lethal.
It mustn't fall into the wrong hands.

255
00:21:24,783 --> 00:21:28,776
I'm think of getting a food taster,
all this tasteless poison about.

256
00:21:30,856 --> 00:21:32,983
- What do you think?
- Good idea.

257
00:21:33,058 --> 00:21:34,821
Hmm.

258
00:21:35,961 --> 00:21:38,828
Maybe I'll eat half an hour after you do.

259
00:22:20,639 --> 00:22:22,630
What have you got for me?

260
00:22:26,445 --> 00:22:28,936
What's the matter?

261
00:22:29,014 --> 00:22:30,982
A conscience?

262
00:22:34,286 --> 00:22:37,483
- How much for this?
- Depends what this is.

263
00:22:37,589 --> 00:22:40,717
This is a letter to King Richard from Robin,

264
00:22:40,792 --> 00:22:44,990
telling him all about you and the Sheriff
and the Black Knights.

265
00:22:46,431 --> 00:22:48,399
Game'd be up, eh, Gisborne?

266
00:22:48,467 --> 00:22:51,595
- Give me that.
- I can't.

267
00:22:51,670 --> 00:22:55,868
I told Robin I'd give it to Roger of Stoke.
He's coming to take it to the King.

268
00:22:55,974 --> 00:22:59,466
- What's your proposal?
- I'll give it to him, then I'm clean.

269
00:22:59,578 --> 00:23:03,674
You can arrest him somewhere out of
town, I don't know anything about it.

270
00:23:05,016 --> 00:23:07,382
Good. You're learning...

271
00:23:07,452 --> 00:23:09,386
Allan.

272
00:23:16,828 --> 00:23:19,558
Hey! Stop!

273
00:23:20,265 --> 00:23:23,063
I've seen you!

274
00:23:23,168 --> 00:23:24,658
Ugh!

275
00:23:24,770 --> 00:23:26,897
No, you haven't.

276
00:23:32,744 --> 00:23:36,646
- Come on in, keep your strength up.
- All right. Thanks, Joseph.

277
00:23:36,748 --> 00:23:37,737
Robin.

278
00:23:37,816 --> 00:23:40,580
- Robin!
- Marian. What are you doing here?

279
00:23:40,652 --> 00:23:43,780
- Someone's impersonating me.
- I know.

280
00:23:43,855 --> 00:23:47,985
- I think he's giving out poisoned pies.
- What? In my name?

281
00:23:48,059 --> 00:23:50,892
It's the Sheriff's doing - but why?

282
00:23:50,962 --> 00:23:54,955
I've no idea, unless it's to damage
the Nightwatchman's reputation.

283
00:23:55,033 --> 00:23:58,469
But then he'd blame the Nightwatchman
and he hasn't.

284
00:24:07,312 --> 00:24:10,042
I need to go and see if Jess is all right.

285
00:24:49,688 --> 00:24:52,179
Mm. Smells good.

286
00:24:52,257 --> 00:24:53,690
Are you a cook?

287
00:24:53,792 --> 00:24:57,228
- No, I'm a man of science.
- Science?

288
00:24:57,295 --> 00:24:59,525
What sort of science?

289
00:24:59,598 --> 00:25:02,431
The science of elimination.

290
00:25:02,501 --> 00:25:05,732
- What's that?
- Finding ways to get rid of dirt.

291
00:25:05,804 --> 00:25:09,205
There's dirt everywhere.
We have to get rid of it.

292
00:25:09,274 --> 00:25:13,210
People who will make
the necessary difficult decisions,

293
00:25:13,278 --> 00:25:17,271
- who don't need to be popular.
- You should talk to the Sheriff.

294
00:25:18,283 --> 00:25:22,242
With the right tool,
we can clean this country,

295
00:25:22,320 --> 00:25:24,379
create a new England.

296
00:25:28,727 --> 00:25:31,355
You should definitely talk to the Sheriff.

297
00:25:38,670 --> 00:25:41,070
Food!

298
00:25:43,975 --> 00:25:46,068
- Food.
- I'll take over.

299
00:25:57,222 --> 00:26:00,453
- Did you organize this?
- We had hospitals in the Holy Land.

300
00:26:02,460 --> 00:26:04,394
I didn't think I'd see one again.

301
00:26:04,462 --> 00:26:07,659
How did you know
there wasn't an infectious disease?

302
00:26:08,633 --> 00:26:11,101
- I didn't.
- That's brave.

303
00:26:13,838 --> 00:26:16,466
- How did you know?
- I didn't.

304
00:26:18,476 --> 00:26:20,307
Robin. You eating?

305
00:26:20,412 --> 00:26:22,778
In a moment. The others can start.

306
00:26:22,847 --> 00:26:24,838
No - I need you.

307
00:26:26,084 --> 00:26:28,211
I mean, you should eat.

308
00:26:30,155 --> 00:26:32,419
I'll be there in a moment.

309
00:26:35,026 --> 00:26:37,392
Robin, Robin, I know that man.

310
00:26:37,462 --> 00:26:39,453
I've seen him before in the castle.

311
00:26:39,531 --> 00:26:42,056
He's advising the Sheriff.

312
00:26:44,035 --> 00:26:46,868
And the Lord said, "Take, eat -

313
00:26:46,972 --> 00:26:48,963
do this in memory of me. "

314
00:26:49,040 --> 00:26:51,634
You make it sound like the Last Supper.

315
00:26:56,781 --> 00:26:58,749
- Robin!
- This is the Last Supper.

316
00:26:58,817 --> 00:27:00,808
For you, Joseph.

317
00:27:00,885 --> 00:27:04,878
You poison people and then you keep
a record of their suffering.

318
00:27:06,057 --> 00:27:08,025
What? That is revolting.

319
00:27:08,093 --> 00:27:12,029
My poison has no taste, no color, no odor.

320
00:27:12,097 --> 00:27:14,292
It's a beautiful thing.

321
00:27:14,399 --> 00:27:16,959
What's the cure for the poison?

322
00:27:21,006 --> 00:27:23,566
There are people out there dying.

323
00:27:23,642 --> 00:27:25,166
Children!

324
00:27:26,444 --> 00:27:30,642
It's made from an extract of the Amanita
mushroom - the angel of death.

325
00:27:33,618 --> 00:27:35,984
The devil's cap.

326
00:27:37,622 --> 00:27:39,021
There is no cure.

327
00:27:43,528 --> 00:27:45,223
Stop him!

328
00:27:45,296 --> 00:27:47,457
Open the gate!

329
00:27:47,532 --> 00:27:50,524
Stop that man! Stop that man!

330
00:27:50,635 --> 00:27:53,570
- Stop him!
- It's me! Let me through, it's me!

331
00:27:54,873 --> 00:27:58,036
Stop him! Stop him!

332
00:27:58,109 --> 00:27:59,406
Aarrgghhh!

333
00:28:07,018 --> 00:28:08,918
- They knew him!
- Tricked us!

334
00:28:09,020 --> 00:28:12,148
- Clever.
- Clever? He poisoned us.

335
00:28:12,223 --> 00:28:15,659
- What about these people?
- Belladonna.

336
00:28:15,727 --> 00:28:18,161
- Bella what?
- Belladonna.

337
00:28:18,229 --> 00:28:21,858
- For mushroom poisoning.
- Belladonna is deadly nightshade.

338
00:28:21,966 --> 00:28:25,527
- It is a poison.
- It works. Woodman's remedy.

339
00:28:25,603 --> 00:28:27,537
A poison to fight a poison.

340
00:28:38,149 --> 00:28:40,982
Djaq, Djaq, it's Jess, I think she's going.

341
00:28:45,190 --> 00:28:47,351
- What's that?
- It's a hunch.

342
00:28:47,425 --> 00:28:49,985
But it could kill her.

343
00:28:50,061 --> 00:28:52,393
- Whose hunch?
- Mine.

344
00:28:56,034 --> 00:28:57,399
Here.

345
00:29:00,672 --> 00:29:02,572
Trust me. Let me do this.

346
00:29:16,955 --> 00:29:19,617
She's going anyway, just try it, just try it.

347
00:29:31,970 --> 00:29:33,665
Jess! No!

348
00:29:44,816 --> 00:29:46,010
No!

349
00:29:53,224 --> 00:29:54,316
Jess?

350
00:29:55,493 --> 00:29:57,961
Oh, it's working! It's working.

351
00:29:59,798 --> 00:30:02,266
I think it is - it is working.

352
00:30:02,367 --> 00:30:03,857
Oh!

353
00:30:07,906 --> 00:30:09,931
Oh, merciful God.

354
00:30:10,008 --> 00:30:13,205
- How did you know that?
- I know some things.

355
00:30:13,278 --> 00:30:16,372
We have to stop Joseph poisoning
anybody else.

356
00:30:16,447 --> 00:30:20,315
- We have to get in to the castle.
- How did Will get in?

357
00:30:20,385 --> 00:30:23,047
- Will?
- He's in the castle.

358
00:30:24,255 --> 00:30:27,816
- Didn't you know?
- Oh, no.

359
00:30:27,892 --> 00:30:31,589
- What's going on?
- He's going to kill the Sheriff.

360
00:30:31,663 --> 00:30:35,759
- But Prince John will destroy Nottingham.
- He knows but...

361
00:30:35,834 --> 00:30:38,997
The man the Sheriff killed
was Will's father.

362
00:30:53,451 --> 00:30:56,545
- Roger.
- Where's Robin?

363
00:30:59,090 --> 00:31:01,752
He couldn't make it
but he gave me this for you.

364
00:31:01,826 --> 00:31:03,726
Oh!

365
00:31:03,795 --> 00:31:07,390
- God save the King!
- Yeah. And the rest of us.

366
00:31:25,817 --> 00:31:30,277
Ah! Success with the pitiful of Pitt Street?

367
00:31:30,388 --> 00:31:33,983
Oh, yes. Even those
who hardly touched the food are in agony.

368
00:31:34,058 --> 00:31:37,391
Those who ate the full dose
have begun to die, as I predicted.

369
00:31:39,464 --> 00:31:41,625
Very good. Well done.

370
00:31:41,699 --> 00:31:44,600
- Thank you. Goodbye.
- Pardon?

371
00:31:44,669 --> 00:31:48,264
You can go, back to wherever it was
you came from. You'll be paid.

372
00:31:48,373 --> 00:31:52,036
But the application of my invention -
we're doing that together,

373
00:31:52,110 --> 00:31:55,739
to rid the country of the weak
and the dirty and the parasites.

374
00:31:55,813 --> 00:32:00,011
My dear boy, those are the ones
who do exactly what I tell them to.

375
00:32:00,084 --> 00:32:01,574
We need those.

376
00:32:01,653 --> 00:32:04,952
No, no, no. Your poison should be used on
the King's army

377
00:32:05,023 --> 00:32:08,652
- when he lands on the south coast.
- That's not what we agreed.

378
00:32:08,760 --> 00:32:10,751
Yes. Yes, I know.

379
00:32:10,828 --> 00:32:13,854
And life is usually so much fairer.

380
00:32:15,600 --> 00:32:16,965
Ha!

381
00:32:17,035 --> 00:32:20,368
Come to Daddy!

382
00:32:22,106 --> 00:32:23,334
Nobody passes.

383
00:32:23,408 --> 00:32:26,844
Master Joseph asked us
to bring the body to t'castle.

384
00:32:26,911 --> 00:32:29,106
- What for?
- He didn't say.

385
00:32:30,648 --> 00:32:33,048
Or do you wanna take it?

386
00:32:43,861 --> 00:32:45,453
Enter!

387
00:32:47,065 --> 00:32:48,862
I will not let you use my poison!

388
00:32:50,868 --> 00:32:53,268
I'm surprised to hear you say that, hmm?

389
00:32:53,371 --> 00:32:55,236
A clue.

390
00:32:55,306 --> 00:33:00,767
Luckily, I managed to commandeer
your meticulous records.

391
00:33:01,913 --> 00:33:05,314
- You used me.
- Yes, I used you.

392
00:33:05,850 --> 00:33:07,374
Oh!

393
00:33:08,386 --> 00:33:11,753
You'll just have to bite the bullet.
I like you.

394
00:33:11,823 --> 00:33:17,784
If I didn't, I could make you drink
from your own cup, so to speak.

395
00:33:19,530 --> 00:33:22,431
So, chin-chin, hmm?

396
00:33:24,435 --> 00:33:26,426
Erm, you, you, boy.

397
00:33:28,239 --> 00:33:31,834
- Don't I know you?
- You knew my dad, Dan.

398
00:33:31,909 --> 00:33:35,367
- He's dead now.
- Oh, really?

399
00:33:35,446 --> 00:33:40,406
Well, here's to your
dearly departed dead dad Dan.

400
00:33:43,454 --> 00:33:46,446
Mm. Come along, joy boy, drink up.

401
00:33:48,226 --> 00:33:50,786
And then get lost, hmm?

402
00:33:50,862 --> 00:33:53,057
Otherwise I might change my mind.

403
00:33:53,164 --> 00:33:54,722
To dead Dan!

404
00:34:07,078 --> 00:34:10,206
Raise the gate! Body for Mr. Joseph.

405
00:34:24,028 --> 00:34:26,724
- What's happening?
- Will's in here.

406
00:34:26,798 --> 00:34:32,361
- And he wants to kill the Sheriff.
- And the Sheriff has hired a poisoner.

407
00:34:32,437 --> 00:34:36,032
- Did you see Roger of Stoke?
- Yeah, I gave him your letter.

408
00:34:36,140 --> 00:34:37,539
Good work.

409
00:34:40,645 --> 00:34:44,706
John, Allan, you go down that way.

410
00:34:44,782 --> 00:34:47,580
What do we do if he doesn't come quietly?

411
00:34:47,685 --> 00:34:50,677
- Then you make him.
- But what if he won't?

412
00:34:51,622 --> 00:34:53,886
Whatever it takes, Much.

413
00:34:53,958 --> 00:34:55,926
Whatever it takes?

414
00:34:56,594 --> 00:34:59,495
- Whatever it takes.
- We kill one of our own?

415
00:35:04,769 --> 00:35:06,669
Let's hope we have a choice.

416
00:35:20,151 --> 00:35:22,085
Help!

417
00:35:24,589 --> 00:35:29,288
- Will.
- Robin, help - poison.

418
00:35:29,360 --> 00:35:34,127
Well, according to your friend here,
there is no cure.

419
00:35:34,198 --> 00:35:37,725
So you're gonna die.

420
00:35:37,802 --> 00:35:40,703
No, no, I'm can't die - I'm too young.

421
00:35:40,771 --> 00:35:42,170
Ahh!

422
00:35:43,474 --> 00:35:46,034
And I haven't finished yet.

423
00:35:49,780 --> 00:35:53,113
Dan Scarlett hadn't finished either,
when you killed him.

424
00:35:53,184 --> 00:35:55,778
Him? Dead dad?

425
00:35:56,754 --> 00:36:00,747
The father? I'm gonna die
because a complete nonentity...

426
00:36:00,825 --> 00:36:03,726
And life is usually so much fairer.

427
00:36:06,164 --> 00:36:09,190
- Why, Sheriff?
- Operation Sharmat.

428
00:36:09,267 --> 00:36:11,929
- Oh.
- The King's army.

429
00:36:12,003 --> 00:36:16,633
You shall prove we win but only...

430
00:36:16,741 --> 00:36:18,504
Well, you're not winning now,

431
00:36:18,576 --> 00:36:20,441
- are you?
- No, no, no.

432
00:36:20,545 --> 00:36:24,675
Now, if by the slightest chance...

433
00:36:25,850 --> 00:36:28,114
I happened to have a cure...

434
00:36:28,186 --> 00:36:30,313
would you give up Sharmat?

435
00:36:30,388 --> 00:36:32,982
- No! There is no cure!
- Shut up!

436
00:36:33,090 --> 00:36:35,354
Yes, yes, yes, Robin.

437
00:36:35,426 --> 00:36:38,953
Yes, yes? Well, don't die before I get back.

438
00:36:39,030 --> 00:36:40,497
- No.
- No.

439
00:36:44,769 --> 00:36:46,669
Will!

440
00:36:46,737 --> 00:36:50,104
- You haven't done anything stupid?
- Stupid?

441
00:36:50,174 --> 00:36:53,473
- To the Sheriff.
- I haven't touched him.

442
00:36:53,544 --> 00:36:57,913
It's not pestilence, it's poison
and we have a cure - Little John's idea.

443
00:36:57,982 --> 00:36:59,950
That's... that's good.

444
00:37:00,017 --> 00:37:03,350
You're not happy?
The sick are getting better.

445
00:37:03,421 --> 00:37:05,889
What are you doing?

446
00:37:05,957 --> 00:37:08,949
- My dad isn't getting better!
- Don't do this!

447
00:37:13,998 --> 00:37:16,489
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa. Where's Djaq?

448
00:37:16,567 --> 00:37:18,296
We split up.

449
00:37:20,805 --> 00:37:22,932
- Will's poisoned the Sheriff.
- What?

450
00:37:23,007 --> 00:37:24,770
Djaq's got the remedy.

451
00:37:24,842 --> 00:37:25,968
Will!

452
00:37:29,847 --> 00:37:33,977
- I know what you've done.
- The right thing, that's what I've done.

453
00:37:34,051 --> 00:37:36,781
- Justice in a bottle.
- Djaq has the remedy.

454
00:37:36,854 --> 00:37:40,221
- She told me.
- What have you done with her?

455
00:37:40,324 --> 00:37:44,920
I've stopped the Sheriff. It's what we
all should've done a long time ago.

456
00:37:44,996 --> 00:37:49,194
- Even if all of Nottingham dies?
- That's not my fault.

457
00:37:51,936 --> 00:37:53,198
Whoa, master, no!

458
00:37:53,271 --> 00:37:55,239
- Robin!
- Robin!

459
00:37:55,339 --> 00:37:56,704
Robin!

460
00:37:56,774 --> 00:37:59,607
You wanna watch people die,
you can start with me.

461
00:37:59,710 --> 00:38:02,201
- I can't let the Sheriff live.
- Yes, you can.

462
00:38:02,313 --> 00:38:04,110
My dad - he did it for me.

463
00:38:04,181 --> 00:38:06,809
He stood up to the Sheriff
to prove himself to me.

464
00:38:06,917 --> 00:38:08,782
Then prove yourself to him.

465
00:38:08,853 --> 00:38:11,617
Show them we are stronger men
than the Sheriff.

466
00:38:14,425 --> 00:38:15,585
Robin!

467
00:38:15,693 --> 00:38:18,526
Will! Will, come on!

468
00:38:18,596 --> 00:38:21,724
- Robin, why did you have to do this?
- To prove my point.

469
00:38:23,334 --> 00:38:26,064
Will Scarlett still
believes in the right thing.

470
00:38:26,137 --> 00:38:28,264
Will, please!

471
00:38:29,407 --> 00:38:31,875
Will, do this.

472
00:38:33,110 --> 00:38:35,601
I'll take you to her.

473
00:38:35,713 --> 00:38:38,511
Go, go to the Sheriff's quarters, go!

474
00:38:38,582 --> 00:38:40,675
I'll see you there.

475
00:38:47,258 --> 00:38:49,317
Whoo!

476
00:38:57,635 --> 00:39:00,934
Who's that? What are you doing?
Come on.

477
00:39:07,445 --> 00:39:11,506
Ooh. Nothing like a taste
of your own medicine, is there?

478
00:39:18,656 --> 00:39:21,591
You have got an announcement to make.

479
00:39:26,997 --> 00:39:28,430
Oh.

480
00:39:29,533 --> 00:39:31,228
People of Nottingham!

481
00:39:31,302 --> 00:39:34,237
There is no pestilence.

482
00:39:37,007 --> 00:39:39,407
It was poison!

483
00:39:39,510 --> 00:39:42,877
An experiment for which I'm...

484
00:39:42,947 --> 00:39:44,608
truly, truly, sorry.

485
00:39:44,715 --> 00:39:49,209
- Sharmat!
- I can't, I'm so weak.

486
00:39:49,320 --> 00:39:52,153
Robin! Djaq, the remedy, quick!

487
00:39:52,223 --> 00:39:58,958
Will, this is your call
- prove to me Will Scarlett believes in doing the right thing.

488
00:40:00,297 --> 00:40:02,959
- You didn't drink the poison, did you?
- No.

489
00:40:03,033 --> 00:40:05,866
But I think my point still stands so...

490
00:40:07,705 --> 00:40:09,104
Yeah.

491
00:40:09,173 --> 00:40:11,266
Yeah, it does.

492
00:40:15,045 --> 00:40:17,172
This is to the memory of my good father,

493
00:40:17,248 --> 00:40:19,375
Dan Scarlett,

494
00:40:19,450 --> 00:40:21,748
and the people of Nottingham.

495
00:40:29,260 --> 00:40:31,125
He can't be dead.

496
00:40:33,097 --> 00:40:37,557
This is getting weird. I want him to live,
I don't want him to live.

497
00:40:37,635 --> 00:40:38,602
Come on!

498
00:40:38,669 --> 00:40:42,332
- Just joshing.
- Finish the speech.

499
00:40:42,406 --> 00:40:45,102
Don't think so,
now I've had the remedy, hmm?

500
00:40:45,176 --> 00:40:48,339
- Guards! Guards!
- Go! Go!

501
00:40:48,412 --> 00:40:50,403
Kill him!

502
00:40:51,615 --> 00:40:56,746
Then he looked and saw the angel of death
standing between heaven and earth.

503
00:40:56,821 --> 00:41:00,257
Joseph, there's a cure.
I'll give you the antidote.

504
00:41:00,324 --> 00:41:02,815
I was going to be remembered
for 1,000 years,

505
00:41:02,893 --> 00:41:05,054
the creator of the perfect poison.

506
00:41:05,129 --> 00:41:07,188
There cannot be an antidote.

507
00:41:07,264 --> 00:41:09,994
There is an antidote
and any woodsman knows it.

508
00:41:10,067 --> 00:41:12,399
No!

509
00:41:22,780 --> 00:41:24,304
Hood!

510
00:41:25,282 --> 00:41:27,773
Give me... Give me your hand.

511
00:41:39,497 --> 00:41:40,657
Ahhh!

512
00:41:46,570 --> 00:41:47,537
Get him!

513
00:42:01,752 --> 00:42:03,720
Stop him!

514
00:42:08,759 --> 00:42:10,317
Thank you!

515
00:42:11,328 --> 00:42:13,091
Thank you, Robin.

516
00:42:23,841 --> 00:42:26,810
It's good to have you back, Lukey.
Are you both ready?

517
00:42:26,911 --> 00:42:29,345
What's he doing up there?

518
00:42:29,413 --> 00:42:32,610
I thought you said Will was gonna build
something to remind you of your father.

519
00:42:32,716 --> 00:42:36,174
He is. Wait for the light.

520
00:42:36,253 --> 00:42:38,517
Light?

521
00:42:38,589 --> 00:42:40,557
It is light.

522
00:42:45,729 --> 00:42:47,321
Any second.

523
00:42:49,166 --> 00:42:50,360
Now.

524
00:43:03,881 --> 00:43:04,848
Dan.

525
00:43:07,284 --> 00:43:09,616
That is...

526
00:43:13,023 --> 00:43:14,320
Beautiful.

527
00:43:18,796 --> 00:43:20,593
He was a good man.

528
00:43:20,664 --> 00:43:22,359
Yeah.

529
00:43:23,100 --> 00:43:24,727
Yeah, he was.

